R AMBULANCE FLIGHTS ON ACT MISSIONS. 3. TRANSIENT OPS ARE AUTH FOR SAFETY OF FLT OR TO MEET OPERATIONAL DEMANDS. 4. ACFT MAY NOT LOITER. 5. UAS OPR WHO DO NOT COMPLY WITH APPLICABLE AIRSPACE RESTRICTIONS ARE WARNED THAT PURSUANT TO 10 U.S.C.SECTION 130I AND 6 U.S.C.SECTION 124N, THE DEPARTMENT OF DEFENSE(DOD), THE DEPARTMENT OF HOMELAND SECURITY(DHS) OR THE DEPARTMENT OF JUSTICE(DOJ) MAY TAKE SECURITY ACTION THAT RESULTS IN THE INTERFERENCE, DISRUPTION, SEIZURE, DAMAGING, OR DESTRUCTION OF UNMANNED ACFT DEEMED TO POSE A CREDIBLE SAFETY OR SECURITY THREAT TO PROTECTED PERSONNEL, FAC, OR ASSETS. 6. THE SYSTEM OPERATIONS SUPPORT CENTER (SOSC), IS THE CDN FAC FOR UAS OPS, SUBMIT SGI WAIVER REQUEST VIA HTTPS://WAIVERS.FAA.GOV, FIRST RESPONDERS EMGERGENCY OPS CTC THE SOSC AT 202-267-8276. 7. THE FAA RECOMMENDS THAT ALL ACFT OPR CK NOTAMS FREQUENTLY FOR POSSIBLE CHANGES TO THIS TFR PRIOR TO OPS. OPR MAY REVIEW THE TFR DETAILS AT HTTPS://TFR.FAA.GOV/ OR HTTPS://WWW.1800WXBRIEF.COM. 2611251600-2611251930","area_km2":266.5,"ceiling_ft":4999,"floor_ft":0,"hours":3.5,"impact":"moderate","impact_basis":["266 km2"],"nearest_core30":{"airport":"DTW","km":262.4}},"subject_id":"cordon:tfr:6-9639","event_start":"2026-11-25T16:00:00Z","event_end":"2026-11-25T19:30:00Z","last_change":"new","last_change_at":"2026-11-24T00:42:45Z","subdivisions":["US-OH"],"valid_until":"2026-11-25T19:30:00Z","place_basis":"location","sea_areas":[]}}}
